WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.690
<v Speaker 1>This is Jonathan Becker reporting to you from magicgathering.com. We're here with Hall of Famer Bob Maher. Junior. How you doing, Bob?</v>

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:06.530
<v Speaker 2>I'm doing great.</v>

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.490
<v Speaker 1>Tell me, how did it feel to be up there and being a doctor, the whole thing?</v>

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:30.890
<v Speaker 2>Felt great magic spending huge part of my life for so many years. It just it felt wonderful to get recognized as as excelling at the game. Like it. It makes me feel like I wasn't just spinning my wheels. I got to stand up on stage. See, the other people I got inducted with who are also kind of part of my life have spent so much time with them and also looking down in the audience and seeing my parents and my kids and my wife.</v>

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:34.820
<v Speaker 2>It was just, it was a very nice moment for me, kind of bringing together a lot of different periods in my life.</v>

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:42.060
<v Speaker 1>Had to be. It seems very exciting to me, like you've got a lot of great memories in the Pro Tour. Obviously, being a Hall of Fame player, what's what's your very favorite one?</v>

00:00:43.510 --> 00:01:09.530
<v Speaker 2>Most of my favorite memories come from the team competitions. One of my favorite memories probably has to be making the top four with Gary Wise and Neil Reeves. I always have a lot more fun in the team tournaments if someone to celebrate your success with. Another one of my favorite memories is winning the pro turn Chicago. Of course, I was a was a really tough match that by all rights I probably should have lost. So it's even kind of a sweeter victory because I actually played better in order to win it.</v>

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.810
<v Speaker 1>Seemed almost like a movie. As soon as you want in, Courtney came jumping into your arms. There was.</v>

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:31.940
<v Speaker 2>It was, it was a, it was a great moment, Yeah. It was really special. Other than that, like the year I want or the the event I won player of the year was when I got second at Worlds and I lost it. John in the finals was also very good friend of mine. That's also a special moment for me. Like we were in the finals, like I won player of the year. He was world champion. It was just, it was a very nice moment.</v>

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:38.240
<v Speaker 1>Not playing a ton of magically, but moving on to other things in life. Now you have a permanent invitation. Should we expect to see you more?</v>

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:42.800
<v Speaker 2>You'll certainly see more because I haven't been around whatsoever, but</v>

00:01:42.910 --> 00:02:06.330
<v Speaker 2>it might be kind of restricted to domestic pro tours, like maybe one a year. Just if it falls well in my schedule, I'll definitely show up. I never stopped playing Magic because I didn't enjoy it. I was just, I had a lot of other demands on my life, especially having kids, being married and things like that. And it was just one of those things I kind of had to prioritize my life and I made Magic priority for nearly ten years. I kind of had to juggle things just to try and balance my life out.</v>

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:12.150
<v Speaker 1>And you started off 10 today. So what's your over under on? We're gonna finish this weekend.</v>

